{
  "name": "Release notes writer from commit messages",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "hours",
              "hoursInterval": 6
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "b858b805-2ff3-5276-a418-a8db63e3d33b",
      "name": "Schedule",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "raw",
        "jsonOutput": "{\n  \"config\": {\n    \"sheet_url\": \"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/YOUR_SHEET_ID/edit\",\n    \"sheet_tab\": \"Releases\",\n    \"owner_email\": \"you@example.com\",\n    \"business_name\": \"Your Business\",\n    \"sender_name\": \"Your Name\",\n    \"rows_per_run\": 5\n  }\n}",
        "includeOtherFields": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "614e6f70-1f7c-543f-85ba-15ddbd3658ad",
      "name": "Settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        240,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "read",
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "url",
          "value": "={{ $('Settings').first().json.config.sheet_url }}"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "={{ $('Settings').first().json.config.sheet_tab }}"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "a956e25d-fa3b-595e-8329-043dae40da3a",
      "name": "Read rows",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 4.7,
      "position": [
        480,
        0
      ],
      "alwaysOutputData": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const cfg = $('Settings').first().json.config;\nconst has = (v) => v !== undefined && v !== null && String(v).trim() !== '';\nreturn $input.all().filter((i) => has(i.json.raw_changes) && !has(i.json[\"release_notes\"])).slice(0, Number(cfg.rows_per_run));"
      },
      "id": "733ce930-1d42-5852-bb6a-09d8d6e7a9e1",
      "name": "Find rows to fill in",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        720,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Turn these raw changes for version {{ $json.version }} into friendly release notes for customers: group into New, Improved and Fixed, plain language, no internal jargon, only what is listed.\n\n{{ $json.raw_changes }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true
      },
      "id": "a3d527b7-c7df-5687-84b5-6a1813d195dd",
      "name": "AI: fill in the row",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.7,
      "position": [
        960,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "gpt-5-mini",
          "cachedResultName": "gpt-5-mini"
        },
        "responsesApiEnabled": false,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "19a4b985-533d-5e5c-89d8-d3c8bd6086d4",
      "name": "AI model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        960,
        220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsonSchemaExample": "{\n  \"release_notes\": \"New: ...\\nImproved: ...\\nFixed: ...\"\n}"
      },
      "id": "50593d3f-6870-5f9f-a8f2-41aea8916329",
      "name": "AI output format",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        1160,
        220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "return $input.all().map((item, i) => ({ json: { row_number: $('Find rows to fill in').all()[i].json.row_number, ...item.json.output } }));"
      },
      "id": "7e8199ad-2d5c-50d6-911e-e96436e9db99",
      "name": "Match results to rows",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1200,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "update",
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "url",
          "value": "={{ $('Settings').first().json.config.sheet_url }}"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "={{ $('Settings').first().json.config.sheet_tab }}"
        },
        "columns": {
          "mappingMode": "autoMapInputData",
          "value": {},
          "matchingColumns": [
            "row_number"
          ],
          "schema": []
        },
        "options": {
          "cellFormat": "RAW",
          "handlingExtraData": "ignoreIt"
        }
      },
      "id": "1aa49e4a-8ae7-50dd-83d7-b184a52fefea",
      "name": "Write back to the sheet",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 4.7,
      "position": [
        1440,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Release notes writer from commit messages\nPaste commit messages or ticket titles into a sheet row. AI turns them into friendly, customer-facing release notes.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "3f82018d-dcd1-5f3d-87dd-15c4eaec7efd",
      "name": "Note: what this does",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Setup (about 10 minutes)\n1. Use a Google Sheet with a tab named **Releases** and these headers in row 1 (see `sheet-headers.csv`).\n2. Fill the input columns (raw_changes). Leave release_notes empty: the AI fills it.\n3. Open **Settings**: sheet URL and how many rows to process per run.\n4. Connect Google Sheets and OpenAI on the nodes with warnings.\n5. Run once by hand, check the results, then switch to **Active**. It only touches rows where release_notes is empty.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "daa93a8e-cabd-58b3-b37b-f31eb5d280e5",
      "name": "Note: setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        400,
        -400
      ]
    }
